<?xml version="1.0"?>
<rdf:RDF xmlns="https://in2use.com/process_model#"
     xml:base="https://in2use.com/process_model"
     xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"
     xmlns:mod="https://w3id.org/mod#"
     xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#"
     xmlns:pav="http://purl.org/pav/"
     xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
     xmlns:xml="http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace"
     xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#"
     xmlns:dcat="http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#"
     xmlns:foaf="http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/"
     xmlns:prov="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#"
     xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"
     xmlns:skos="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#"
     xmlns:sulo="https://w3id.org/sulo/"
     xmlns:swrl="http://www.w3.org/2003/11/swrl#"
     xmlns:time="http://www.w3.org/2006/time#"
     xmlns:vann="http://purl.org/vocab/vann/"
     xmlns:swrla="http://swrl.stanford.edu/ontologies/3.3/swrla.owl#"
     xmlns:swrlb="http://www.w3.org/2003/11/swrlb#"
     xmlns:terms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/"
     xmlns:p-plan="http://purl.org/net/p-plan#"
     xmlns:schema="https://schema.org/"
     xmlns:process_model="https://in2use.com/process_model/">
    <owl:Ontology rdf:about="https://in2use.com/process_model">
        <terms:created rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-10-22</terms:created>
        <terms:creator rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8824-9577"/>
        <terms:description xml:lang="en">Self-contained experimental process ontology combining a collaborative tendering plan and its synthetic execution, the abstract Method Omega development methodology, temporal reasoning examples, and provisional state and goal tests. The ontology IRI is https://in2use.com/process_model; project-defined entities use the namespace https://in2use.com/process_model/. Reused external vocabulary retains its original IRIs. The model includes ten SWRL rules and SPARQL tests; it does not implement a workflow engine. No Method Omega execution, LLM evaluation record or materialized inference is included.</terms:description>
        <terms:modified rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-11-18</terms:modified>
        <terms:source rdf:resource="https://doi.org/10.1080/00207543.2023.2242508"/>
        <terms:source rdf:resource="https://in2use.com/process_model/Source_Schema_Metadata"/>
        <terms:source rdf:resource="https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model"/>
        <terms:title xml:lang="en">Process model with examples</terms:title>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Process model with examples</rdfs:label>
        <owl:versionInfo>process-model-v4-2026-11-18</owl:versionInfo>
        <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">2026-10-22 — Changed by ChatGPT. Implemented Figure 8 as a separate planned collaboration on the updated supply-chain schema. Added placeholder organizations, contextual role instances, seven task definitions and planned assignments, five planned events, ten control-flow transitions, ten resource/message variables, four message exchanges, and one explicit exclusive choice with approval and rejection conditions. Preserved the figure&apos;s seven-task structure by documenting t11 as a send-and-await request/reply task. Retained separate initial-draft, contribution, revised tender and submitted-tender variables, and the single-producer P-Plan semantics. The submitted-tender slot is an explicit completion artifact chosen for this model. Preserved all ten existing SWRL rules. No runtime execution, branch-selection result, synthetic test data or inferred assertions are included.</skos:changeNote>
        <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">2026-10-23 - Changed by ChatGPT. Corrected the inherited dcterms:created metadata value from 2025-28-11 to 2025-11-28 (interpreted as 28 November 2025) to address the reported AllegroGraph import error. Workflow definitions and rules are unchanged.</skos:changeNote>
        <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">2026-11-05 (ChatGPT): Completed the reused PROV-O subset for qualified usage by copying the standard declarations of Usage, EntityInfluence, qualifiedUsage, entity, qualifiedInfluence and influencer, including their original domain/range and hierarchy axioms. This prevents qualifiedUsage and entity being interpreted as annotation properties by OWLAPI. Existing data, rules and vocabulary IRIs are unchanged.</skos:changeNote>
        <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">2026-11-05 (ChatGPT): Restored ten complete SWRL rules and variable declarations from supply_chain_model(1).ttl, removed damaged SWRL structures and structural annotation-property declarations, and added a synthetic approved execution with six StepExecutions, one enclosing run Activity, seven OWL-Time intervals, ten realized resource variables and qualified PROV associations/usages. Preserved prior plan assertions and inverse-property edits. No inferred assertions or SHACL constraints added.</skos:changeNote>
        <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">2026-11-06 (ChatGPT): Added the Method Omega excerpt in the https://www.in2use.com/method_omega/ namespace, preserving existing domain data and all ten SWRL rules. Copied four missing standard P-Plan terms from the 2014 release. Added has_step and precedes display inverses, Finish_To_Start_Transition, exposes_output_variable, and expected_duration in https://www.in2use.com/process_model/. Kept separate MultiSteps and body Plans, single producers for Variables, and conditional rework without a precedence cycle. No Method Omega Activities, duration values, SHACL constraints or materialized inferences added. Updated ontology-level descriptive metadata; retained the ontology IRI.</skos:changeNote>
        <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">2026-11-18 (ChatGPT): Added provisional State Description and Goal vocabulary, goal decomposition, reusable test specifications, controlled evaluation methods/results, and evaluation-record vocabulary in https://www.in2use.com/process_model/. Added explicit natural-language definitions to the four existing decision conditions and aligned DecisionCondition to State_Description. Added three deterministic tender tests and an unexecuted ChatGPT requirements-readiness template. Preserved all original example assertions and ten SWRL rules. The eventual higher-level state-description language, including a possible Manchester Syntax extension, remains deferred. No runtime evaluation records or inferred assertions are included.</skos:changeNote>
        <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">2026-11-18 (ChatGPT): Consolidated the ontology identity and all project-defined resources under https://in2use.com/process_model/ (without www). Migrated five project namespaces, nineteen locally created historical-event/date examples previously in the OWL-Time namespace, and seventeen SWRL variables. Kept the Partner Role and Lead Supplier Role classes distinct from the Tendering Partner Role and Tendering Lead Supplier Role individuals. Updated stored queries and supporting files. Preserved external vocabulary IRIs, historical provenance text, dates, axioms and example relationships. Kept rdf:type first in RDF/XML descriptions for OWLAPI compatibility. The ontology IRI remains stable across future versions; this revision is recorded in owl:versionInfo.</skos:changeNote>
        <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">2026-11-18 (ChatGPT): Set the ontology IRI to https://in2use.com/process_model without a trailing slash. Retained https://in2use.com/process_model/ as the entity namespace and pm: prefix. Updated the 54 rdfs:isDefinedBy references in the complete ontology and the 49 matching references in the state/goal review fragment. Updated current documentation and validation expectations. Entity IRIs, labels, logical axioms, SWRL rules, and query text are unchanged.</skos:changeNote>
        <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">2026-11-18 (ChatGPT): Standardized project-defined class and individual IRIs to Title_Case with underscores, and property IRIs to lowercase with underscores and has_/is_..._of naming where applicable. Standardized rule identifiers and English default labels; retained prior labels as alternative labels. Updated queries and supporting files. Preserved external vocabulary, historical provenance, logical meanings, and RDF/XML type-first serialization. Recorded the renaming in docs/naming_migration.tsv.</skos:changeNote>
        <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">2026-11-4 Changed by M. DeBellis. Several P-Plan properties had labels in CamelCase. I added skos:prefLabel values for them using my standard of all lower case for property labels. E.g., pplan:isStepOfPlan had label &quot;isStepOfPlan&quot;. I added a skos pref label: &quot;is step of plan&quot; and made it a lang string datatype.</skos:changeNote>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">Control-flow transitions, message variables and decision conditions are explicit assertions. The existing SWRL rules infer candidate resource dependencies and shared inputs; they neither select a branch nor execute the plan. All declared steps and resource variables are explicitly distinct. Each produced variable has exactly one asserted producer. The call-for-tender variable is supplied externally.</skos:note>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">Figure 8 returns the partner vote to t11SendTenderForVotingTask. This model interprets that task as sending the voting request and awaiting the reply. Consequently t11 and t12 have resource dependencies in both directions; these describe a request/reply exchange, not a control-flow loop or a reason to assert each task precedes the other. An executable refinement may split sending and receiving into separate steps. The replacement branch ends where the figure ends; no retry loop is added.</skos:note>
        <skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Figure 8 plan content follows the cited paper and its accompanying text; the dated tender run is explicitly synthetic. Method Omega follows Michael DeBellis&apos;s supplied diagram and conventions, with modeling choices explained on its individuals. Existing Time examples remain. These are review examples, not a workflow engine or records of real projects.</skos:scopeNote>
        <skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">State/goal extensions are a first draft. SPARQL is a provisional executable representation. The LLM template calls the configured OpenAI model through AllegroGraph and requires actual evidence plus context; it is not a formal condition expression. No LLM was called and no evaluation record was fabricated. The ontology IRI is https://in2use.com/process_model and the entity namespace is https://in2use.com/process_model/; reused external vocabulary keeps its original IRIs.</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Ontology>
    


