        <sulo:isPartOf rdf:resource="https://in2use.com/process_model/Customer_Portal_Plan"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A fictional project plan for developing a customer self-service portal with account access, support requests, and request-status tracking. It is derived from the reusable Method Omega specification. All people, responsibilities, deliverable slots, and dates in this example are illustrative.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Customer Portal Plan</rdfs:label>
        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Customer Portal Plan</skos:prefLabel>
        <skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">The baseline schedule runs from 1 February through 5 March 2027, with explicit UTC-08:00 offsets. It assumes the first requirements review leads to approval; this is a scheduling assumption, not an asserted decision outcome. The rejection and rework branch remains available and would require a revised schedule. No executions, actual document versions, evaluation results, effort estimates, or holiday-calendar calculations are asserted. Composite windows summarize their children and are not additional person-hours. The four opaque later phases retain the abstraction of Method Omega.</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


